WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.203
Hi, I'm Turbo!

00:00:02.203 --> 00:00:05.245
These low-bit quants claim their bits were placed by measurement.

00:00:05.245 --> 00:00:07.375
Here's how, and what the files show.

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:12.908
Measure which parts matter by crushing each one in turn, then spend

00:00:12.908 --> 00:00:14.603
a memory budget where it counts.

00:00:19.317 --> 00:00:23.078
Crush one group of tensors at a time, and measure its KL

00:00:23.078 --> 00:00:26.211
divergence from full precision, against the model's own noise curve.

00:00:26.631 --> 00:00:30.495
Then allocate bits to minimise KL within the target machine's memory.

00:00:30.915 --> 00:00:34.431
Each tensor's type is written in the header, readable without the weights.

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:39.415
In the largest file, every block gets the same type.

00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:40.389
No per-layer structure.

00:00:40.809 --> 00:00:44.638
In the three smaller files, blocks zero, one, sixty-three and sixty-four

00:00:44.638 --> 00:00:46.030
keep the primary type.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:49.511
Blocks two to sixty-two crush their gate and up weights.

00:00:49.931 --> 00:00:51.707
Same keep-set at three budgets.

00:00:51.707 --> 00:00:56.681
A knapsack re-solved per budget would not normally do that; a first-and-last rule would.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.009
Demoting attention keys and values saves eleven megabytes of seven point three

00:01:03.009 --> 00:01:05.697
four gigabytes, from the most sensitive tensors.

00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:10.540
Demoting the feed-forward gate and up saves seven hundred and sixty-five megabytes.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.015
That's the real lever.

00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:15.844
No file weighs what its name says.

00:01:15.844 --> 00:01:19.633
The one named one point seven five measures one point nine oh

00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:22.791
six: its output head alone is thirteen point four percent.

00:01:24.142 --> 00:01:27.430
The filename is marketing; the tensor-info block at the top of the

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.527
file is the build.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.984
To recap: measure, fit, and then check the header, because the

00:01:34.984 --> 00:01:36.121
header is the build.

00:01:36.541 --> 00:01:38.572
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:38.572 --> 00:01:39.152
I'm Turbo.

00:01:39.152 --> 00:01:39.442
Bye!
